@ref art 10(4) (src:135)
`art 10(4): regulation 25(1)(a) of the Statutory Neonatal Care Pay (General) Regulations 2025, the weekly rate of statutory neonatal care pay` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 187.18, 194.32


@ref arts 8 to 10 (src:125-135)
DECLARE `a kind of statutory pay whose weekly rate arts 8 to 10 state` IS ONE OF
    `statutory sick pay`
    `statutory maternity pay`
    `statutory paternity pay`
    `statutory adoption pay`
    `statutory shared parental pay`
    `statutory parental bereavement pay`
    `statutory neonatal care pay`

@ref arts 8 to 10 (src:125-135)
GIVEN `which one` IS A `a kind of statutory pay whose weekly rate arts 8 to 10 state`
GIVETH A `a sum and its replacement`
`arts 8 to 10: the replaced and the replacing weekly rate` `which one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which one`
    WHEN `statutory sick pay` THEN `art 8: section 157(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act, the weekly rate of statutory sick pay`
    WHEN `statutory maternity pay` THEN `art 9: regulation 6 of the Statutory Maternity Pay (General) Regulations 1986, the prescribed weekly rate of statutory maternity pay`
    WHEN `statutory paternity pay` THEN `art 10(1)(a): regulation 2(a) of the Statutory Paternity Pay and Statutory Adoption Pay (Weekly Rates) Regulations 2002, the weekly rate of statutory paternity pay`
    WHEN `statutory adoption pay` THEN `art 10(1)(b): regulation 3(a) of the Statutory Paternity Pay and Statutory Adoption Pay (Weekly Rates) Regulations 2002, the weekly rate of statutory adoption pay`
    WHEN `statutory shared parental pay` THEN `art 10(2): regulation 40(1)(a) of the Statutory Shared Parental Pay (General) Regulations 2014, the weekly rate of statutory shared parental pay`
    WHEN `statutory parental bereavement pay` THEN `art 10(3): regulation 20(1)(a) of the Statutory Parental Bereavement Pay (General) Regulations 2020, the weekly rate of statutory parental bereavement pay`
    WHEN `statutory neonatal care pay` THEN `art 10(4): regulation 25(1)(a) of the Statutory Neonatal Care Pay (General) Regulations 2025, the weekly rate of statutory neonatal care pay`


§ `Article 11 -- Increase in rate of graduated retirement benefit`

-- (1): the sum is in PENCE ("17.83" pence), not pounds: 17.83 pence a week becomes 18.51 pence. The Order says
-- the sum "shall be increased by 3.8 per cent" and that the reference "shall have effect as a reference to 18.51
-- pence": both are stated, so the pair is a value. 17.83 increased by 3.8 per cent is 18.50754 (NOTES.md, F-01).
-- src:136 | 11 Increase in rate of graduated retirement benefit
-- src:137 | (1) In section 36(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965 (graduated retirement benefit)—
-- src:138 | (a) the sum of “17.83” pence shall be increased by 3.8 per cent; and
-- src:139 | (b) the reference to that sum shall have effect as a reference to “18.51” pence.
@ref art 11(1) (src:136-139)
`art 11(1): section 36(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965, the sum of graduated retirement benefit, in pence` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 17.83, 18.51

-- out of text: Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) (No. 2) Regulations 1978 Sch 2: the increase before the Order is an input.
-- src:140 | (2) The sums which are the increases of graduated retirement benefit under Schedule 2 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) (No. 2) Regulations 1978 (increases for deferred retirement) shall be increased by 3.8 per cent.
@ref art 11(2) (src:140)
GIVEN `the increase of graduated retirement benefit under Schedule 2 to the 1978 Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 11(2): the increase for deferred retirement after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the increase of graduated retirement benefit under Schedule 2 to the 1978 Regulations` MEANS
    `the increase of graduated retirement benefit under Schedule 2 to the 1978 Regulations` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)

-- out of text: Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005 Sch 1: the lump sum before the Order is an input.
-- src:141 | (3) The sums which are lump sums to which surviving spouses or civil partners will become entitled under Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005 (increases of graduated retirement benefit and lump sums) shall be increased by 3.8 per cent.
@ref art 11(3) (src:141)
GIVEN `the lump sum under Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 11(3): the lump sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the lump sum under Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005` MEANS
    `the lump sum under Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)

-- out of text: National Insurance Act 1965 s 37(1): the addition before the Order is an input.
-- src:142 | (4) The sums which are the additions under section 37(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965 (additions for widows and widowers) shall be increased by 3.8 per cent.
@ref art 11(4) (src:142)
GIVEN `the addition under section 37(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 11(4): the addition for widows and widowers after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the addition under section 37(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965` MEANS
    `the addition under section 37(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)

DECLARE `a sum that art 11 increases by 3.8 per cent` IS ONE OF
    `an increase of graduated retirement benefit for deferred retirement (Schedule 2 to the 1978 Regulations)`
    `a lump sum for a surviving spouse or civil partner (Schedule 1 to the 2005 Regulations)`
    `an addition for a widow or widower under section 37(1)`
    `a sum not described in art 11(2) to (4)`

-- out of text: Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) (No. 2) Regulations 1978 Sch 2: the increase before the Order is an input.
@ref art 11 (src:136-142)
GIVEN `which sum` IS A `a sum that art 11 increases by 3.8 per cent`
      `the sum before the increase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`art 11(2) to (4): the sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `which sum` `the sum before the increase` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which sum`
    WHEN `an increase of graduated retirement benefit for deferred retirement (Schedule 2 to the 1978 Regulations)` THEN JUST (`art 11(2): the increase for deferred retirement after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the sum before the increase`)
    WHEN `a lump sum for a surviving spouse or civil partner (Schedule 1 to the 2005 Regulations)` THEN JUST (`art 11(3): the lump sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the sum before the increase`)
    WHEN `an addition for a widow or widower under section 37(1)` THEN JUST (`art 11(4): the addition for widows and widowers after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the sum before the increase`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

