@ref art 16(1) (src:160-163)
DECLARE `a sub-paragraph of regulation 10(2) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994` IS ONE OF
    `Incapacity Benefit regulation 10(2)(a)`
    `Incapacity Benefit regulation 10(2)(b)`

@ref art 16(1) (src:160-163)
GIVEN `which one` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 10(2) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994`
GIVETH A `a sum and its replacement`
`art 16(1): the replaced and the replacing sum` `which one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which one`
    WHEN `Incapacity Benefit regulation 10(2)(a)` THEN `art 16(1)(a): regulation 10(2)(a) of the Social Security (Incapacity Benefit) Regulations 1994`
    WHEN `Incapacity Benefit regulation 10(2)(b)` THEN `art 16(1)(b): regulation 10(2)(b) of the Social Security (Incapacity Benefit) Regulations 1994`


-- src:164 | (2) In the case of a claimant entitled to long-term incapacity benefit who was subject to regulation 2(3) of the Employment and Support Allowance (Up-rating Modification) (Transitional) Regulations 2008 the sums specified in regulation 10(2)(a) and (b) of the Social Security (Incapacity Benefit) Regulations 1994 shall be increased to “£15.50” and “£8.60” respectively.
@ref art 16(2) (src:164)
`art 16(2): regulation 10(2)(a) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994, the sum for a claimant subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations` MEANS 15.50

@ref art 16(2) (src:164)
`art 16(2): regulation 10(2)(b) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994, the sum for a claimant subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations` MEANS 8.60

@ref art 16(2) (src:164)
GIVEN `which one` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 10(2) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 16(2): the sum in regulation 10(2) for a claimant subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations` `which one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which one`
    WHEN `Incapacity Benefit regulation 10(2)(a)` THEN `art 16(2): regulation 10(2)(a) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994, the sum for a claimant subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations`
    WHEN `Incapacity Benefit regulation 10(2)(b)` THEN `art 16(2): regulation 10(2)(b) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994, the sum for a claimant subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations`

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance (Up-rating Modification) (Transitional) Regulations 2008 reg 2(3): whether the claimant was subject to it is an input.
@ref art 16 (src:160-164)
GIVEN `which one` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 10(2) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994`
      `the claimant is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit and was subject to regulation 2(3) of the ESA Up-rating Modification Transitional Regulations 2008` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 16: the sum in regulation 10(2) after the Order` `which one` `the claimant is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit and was subject to regulation 2(3) of the ESA Up-rating Modification Transitional Regulations 2008` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit and was subject to regulation 2(3) of the ESA Up-rating Modification Transitional Regulations 2008`
    THEN `art 16(2): the sum in regulation 10(2) for a claimant subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations` `which one`
    ELSE (`art 16(1): the replaced and the replacing sum` `which one`)'s `the sum after the Order`

